v3.8.1
the LitVM LiteForge RPC is Zeeve's https://rpc.testnet.liteforge.zeeve.net/
  (node/.env, networks.ini, the installer's vars): the LiteForge testnet moved
  from Caldera to Zeeve on 2026-11-12 with its chain id, state and contracts,
  and the Caldera endpoints answer 404
every eth_getLogs scan reads at most <NETWORK>_LOGS_CHUNK_BLOCKS blocks per
  call (9000 unless set; 3000 on litvm_liteforge and litvm_liteforge_unsafe,
  whose RPC refuses a wider range): the ESR, broker, cancellation, output-row,
  session-registry, image-registry and placement-time scans share
  utils.block_ranges

v3.8.0
the agent runs on the 1.2 PoX (pox-smart-contract-litvm) beside the legacy
  contracts: at start it probes each network's contract for pricingVersion()
  and, where it answers, binds the reader, the pricing, the reservation broker
  and the ECLD token the contract names (the log line "pox=1.2 reader=...");
  a contract that reverts is legacy and runs as before. polygon_amoy and
  polygon_amoy_unsafe bind the 1.2 implementation
  0x3Aa1A0d7A8A9DaE9e13345D3261afe86D67326A4 (node/.env); the request and
  order caches of a network whose contract address changed start again
the integration test waits INTEGRATION_TEST_SECONDS (900 s, from 300) for the
  trustedzone's result and reads capability.time.etny and capability.etny
  before context_test.etny and the bucket clean-up: the node's capability
  record (its benchmarked compute units, the validators' two time statements
  and the trustedzone's P-384 signature). A record is admitted when a seated
  validator signed both statements, the record names the agent's wallet, the
  trustedzone requires dcap and the cu is within CU_MAX_THOUSANDTHS; it is
  kept in node/<network>/capability.json across restarts, stands seven days
  from its t1 and is re-measured a day before; an -unsafe or sgx trustedzone
  writes no record the agent admits. The integration .env and every order
  .env carry ETNY_NODE_ADDRESS (the wallet adding the DP requests); the first
  order after a new record carries ETNY_PROBE_FIRST=1; ETNY_NGROK_AUTHTOKEN is
  no longer injected
on a 1.2 contract the DP request is addDPRequestV2 with the record's cu and a
  tip per CU-hour: <NETWORK>_TIP_PER_CU_HOUR_WEI (0) plus the node's own gas
  (the DP request, the placement and the started row, from a moving average of
  its status-1 receipts in node/<network>/gas_profile.json, seeded from
  node/gas_profile_seed.json) at the pricing's average gas price, over one
  CU-hour; metadata3 and metadata4 carry the record's fourteen keys (metadata3
  cuval, cun, cut0, cut1, cub0, cub1, cusig0, cusig1; metadata4 cu, cuv, cuat,
  cusig, cuheap, cuworkers, the record's trustedzone first in its list). The
  request is refreshed (refreshDPRequest) an hour before its expiry from the
  idle tick and the enclave wait, re-added when it carries another record or
  the other accept-reserved flag, cancelled in at most CANCEL_ATTEMPTS sends,
  and a request the validators cancelled (DPRequestCancelled) is re-tested
  before the next one. The pre-filter judges a V2 DO request on its recorded
  terms against the reader's quote plus the tip and the node's cu (a reserved
  request is left to the broker, a legacy request is judged with the network,
  validator and publisher fees); a sub-token V2 request, which the legacy
  getter reads as price 0, is still skipped where no quote is read, as every
  3.7.x agent skips it. settlementOf is logged after the result
the relay: the session rows are served before the commits in the enclave-wait
  tick and the final sweep; a row counts on a status-1 receipt; a
  session.commit.<n>.<key16>.<relayNonce>.json is relayed once a
  session.output.<seq>.commits names it and that row's receipt is in,
  esr.commit.*.json as it appears, at most ESR_LEDGER_CAP (256) per order; the
  trustedzone's etny-sw row is relayed on every order. One gas ledger per
  order (orders/<id>/relay.json), the order's chainFeeWei at its
  gasPriceCapWei on a recorded 1.2 order (re-read for a raise), the network's
  <NETWORK>_ESR_RELAY_GAS_BUDGET_WEI on legacy orders only; a relay or result
  whose base fee plus priority fee is above the cap waits ("gas wait" in the
  log), bounded by the order's end; two or more commits of one enclave at a
  tick go as one commitForBatch and two or more pending rows as one
  _addMetadataToDPRequestBatch
the result of a recorded 1.2 order is posted with _addResultToOrderV2 carrying
  the v5 result's commit count and gas sum; the wait for the enclave's
  transaction.txt lasts to the order's deadline while the enclave lives; a
  result held by the gas price past the order's end is sent at the live price
  up to the operator's fee ceiling for RESULT_SEND_GRACE_SECONDS (3600), then
  abandoned with a log line
the reservation broker, on a 1.2 contract that names one (none is deployed
  yet): setAcceptsReserved and commitReserved at every start unless
  <NETWORK>_ACCEPT_RESERVED=0 (true), the window extended while the agent
  runs; an order the broker places on the node's offer approved and run at
  once; <NETWORK>_FARM_INVITE (<farm>:<expiresAt>:<signature>) joins the farm
  with joinFarm, <NETWORK>_FARM_ACCEPT (true) accepts the handovers the farm's
  members and the node's appointers announce; the successor of a handover
  window stages the predecessor's unanswered inputs as session.replay.<seq>
  and the state objects the fence needs as state.<cid>.enc. The handover's
  gas deposit is pulled in ECLD: the node wallet holds the deposit and
  approves the broker for it. `etny-node.py --handover --network <name>
  [--appoint <node>]` asks the running agent to announce the handover of the
  reserved order it runs (node/<network>/handover.json) and prints its
  answer; the agent serves the order to the window, posts the result and
  adds no next DP request. SIGHUP, the unit's KillSignal, does the same while
  a reserved order runs and its announcement is not refused (the drain state
  survives the daily restart) and stops the agent as before otherwise;
  ubuntu/etc/systemd/system/etny-node.service sets TimeoutStopSec=21600 so a
  stop waits for the window, and ubuntu/etny-node-start.sh installs the
  repository's unit when it differs from the installed one
the mirror (REPLICATION_ONLY): probes the contract's generation and binds the
  broker, reads no fee percents and sends nothing; on a broker network it pins
  the artefacts every reservation's template names for the reservation's term
  (esr_progress 'reservation_templates'); the payload intake resolves a
  request whose owner answers ERC-165 for IReservationResolver to the holder
  holderOf names, and refuses one for which it finds no holder
settings: <NETWORK>_TIP_PER_CU_HOUR_WEI, <NETWORK>_ACCEPT_RESERVED,
  <NETWORK>_FARM_INVITE and <NETWORK>_FARM_ACCEPT (above), each defaulted when
  absent; node/.env.example documents every variable
dependency_manager pins cryptography 3.4.8 (the etny-sw row's P-384 check)
the constants of the above are in node/constants.py; the agent's ABI files
  (node/docker/pox.abi the 1.2 union, node/esr.abi, node/reader.abi,
  node/pricing.abi, node/broker.abi, node/resolver.abi, node/erc20.abi) ship
  with the release

v3.7.17
the per-order relay gas budget is a network setting
  (<NETWORK>_ESR_RELAY_GAS_BUDGET_WEI; ESR_RELAY_GAS_BUDGET_WEI, 0.1 of the
  native token, for the networks without one): Polygon Amoy's is 1 POL, a
  metadata row costing about 0.012 POL there, where 0.1 POL held eight
  session output rows
a session row the budget refuses is logged once, not every tick

v3.7.6
the bloxberg testnet and its -unsafe twin run the integration tests of their
  nodenithy trustedzones (etny-nodenithy-testnet,
  etny-nodenithy-testnet-unsafe) after the pynithy ones
a trustedzone with an integration test of its own runs once that test
  passed; one without runs once a passed test covers its platform
  requirement, as before
an order's prerequisites remove the integration bucket, whose .env the
  trustedzones read before the order's own

v3.7.5
the bloxberg testnet and its -unsafe twin read the image registry 0xa372a6e1
  (ECImageRegistryV3, whose securelock names belong to their publishers), and
  the bloxberg testnet's CAS sessions are replicated from the SessionRegistry
  0x44442968, whose records are keyed by name and hash

v3.7.4
a registered image is pinned only when it is an enclave image the Ethernity
  CLOUD SDK builds (scone_image.py): its lib/libbinary-fs.so, the SCONE
  binary-fs, holds the SCONE runtime's variables and the enclave's role
  (securelock or trustedzone), found newest layer first within
  REGISTERED_IMAGE_SCAN_MAX_BYTES (1 GiB) of layer data, decompressing at
  most REGISTERED_IMAGE_INFLATE_MAX_BYTES (2 GiB) and 100,000 archive
  entries; its tree declares at most REGISTERED_IMAGE_MAX_BYTES (3 GiB) and
  its compose REGISTERED_COMPOSE_MAX_BYTES (1 MiB); and the disk keeps
  ESR_MIN_FREE_STORAGE_GB free before the pin, once the declared size is in,
  and while the pin runs; a pin that grows the repository past twice the
  declared size plus 2 GiB is ended and tried again later. Archives are walked
  by the agent itself, header by header, with extended headers over 1 MiB
  refused unread, so no layer makes it hold more than a few MiB
a verdict (verified, refused, unreadable by this agent) stands until those
  bounds or the verifier's version change; an image pinned without a verdict
  is judged in place; a verified image whose pin Kubo no longer holds is
  pinned again, and the retention sweep keeps verified images; a refusal
  unpins only what this replication pinned (pins made by 3.7.2 and 3.7.3 stay),
  sparing a CID another verified image of the network uses
an attempt that fails is tried again after a delay doubling from 10 minutes
  to 6 hours, the entry with the fewest attempts first; one registered-image
  attempt runs at a time in the process
a registered image's publisher is taken only with a canonical base58 peer id,
  added to the peering list only when it is not in it already, and only a
  peering the attempt added is removed after
a registered image and its compose are taken only as the CID text Kubo prints
  for them (varints as go-cid reads them, CIDv1 padding bits zero); an entry
  3.7.2 or 3.7.3 recorded under another spelling is refused, under whatever
  bounds are current
a registration whose strings do not decode is skipped alone
a replication-only agent collects the garbage of refused, unreadable and
  failed attempts at most hourly, while no registered-image pin is in flight
the handles of a network share one esr_progress, written as one snapshot that
  replaces the file
the replication loop runs for the life of the process: the daily restart of
  the order-processing threads stopped it for good

v3.7.0
the -unsafe trustedzones are networks of their own, bloxberg_testnet_unsafe
  and litvm_liteforge_unsafe: the chain and contracts of the network each is
  named after, and only that network's -unsafe trustedzones. A node runs one
  only when it is named: "all", "auto", the installer's AUTO and the legacy
  names select none. An -unsafe network lists only trustedzones ending in
  -unsafe and no other network lists one, or the agent does not start
a node that names a network and its -unsafe twin runs both as one handle on
  their shared protocol contract, with both networks' trustedzones and
  integration tests
litvm_liteforge's trustedzones are provisioned by LitVM's CAS set: the agent
  resolves the CAS from LitVM's validator registry, replicates its session
  registry and peers with its validators' IPFS nodes
the payload intake takes a network's requests under its -unsafe twin's name
  as well
the installer lists LitVM and the two -unsafe networks

v3.6.2
an order placement is simulated before it is sent, and a DO request the
  protocol contract refuses is skipped and cached instead of retried: on
  bloxberg a request whose metadata4 is the zero address cannot be placed
  by any node, and the node re-sent the reverting _placeOrder without end,
  paying gas each time and taking no other request
a placement that is mined but reverted is retried at most three times

v3.6.1
an RPC call on a keep-alive connection the RPC closed while idle is retried
  on a fresh one: web3's default retry missed requests' ConnectionError, so
  the first call after a quiet spell failed with "Remote end closed
  connection without response" (the integration tests' registry reads)

v3.6.0
a node runs the trustedzones whose platform requirement its integration
  tests show it meets: <NETWORK>_TRUSTEDZONE_IMAGES pairs each trustedzone
  with "dcap" (provisioned by a CAS) or "sgx" (the -unsafe testnet variants),
  and <NETWORK>_INTEGRATION_TEST_IMAGES (renamed from
  _INTEGRATION_TEST_IMAGE) lists the images tested
integration tests are tracked per image and a failed one is retried with a
  backoff from 10 minutes doubling to 6 hours, instead of only at the
  daily restart; a test whose image cannot be downloaded cleans up and
  counts as failed
a DO request is skipped, with the reason logged, when the trustedzone it
  names is not one the node runs or its image metadata is not v3;
  process_order refuses such an order after re-running the failed tests
the CAS is resolved only for a compose that names SCONE_CAS_ADDR
a DP request's metadata4 carries the trustedzones the node runs and the
  peer id of its IPFS node
pin retention skips a trustedzone the image registry does not hold
  instead of the whole cleanup round
IPFS_GATEWAY_URL is read from the key node/.env sets
removed the legacy /dev/isgx etny-pynithy composes from node/docker, with
  their Dockerfile, wrapper and result script; the agent used none of them

v3.5.0
fixed result pinning: retries never reconnected, so a stale connection
  flag failed every attempt against a healthy IPFS daemon
one failed pin/ls no longer disables pinning node-wide
serialised IPFS restarts across network threads (lock + 60s cooldown),
  which stops one thread's restart from breaking the others' calls
results that fail to pin are queued on disk and retried after an IPFS
  outage or a node restart, instead of being lost with the process
CAS endpoints are read from CasKeyStore rather than the registry, which
  no longer forwards them (requires a registry exposing keyStore())
3s RPC connect timeout, replacing 120s applied to both phases
HTTP sessions are closed when a network iteration ends
the shared task slot is acquired atomically, so two networks can no
  longer hold it at once or clear each other's ownership

